  "result": "I added `split(cents, parts)` to `shop/money.py` and new tests in `tests/test_money.py`. The full suite passes: 11 tests, 5 of them new.\n\n`split` uses `divmod` to get an even base share, then adds one cent to each of the first few elements until the remainder is used up. So `split(1000, 3)` gives `[334, 333, 333]`. If `parts` is below 1, it raises `ValueError`.\n\nThe new tests cover:\n- an even split\n- remainders of 1 and 2 cents\n- a single part\n- more parts than cents (`split(2, 4)` gives `[1, 1, 0, 0]`)\n- `parts` of 0 and -1 raising `ValueError`\n\n**Negative amounts:** these still add up correctly, but the first elements end up closer to zero, not bigger in size. For example, `split(-10, 3)` gives `[-3, -3, -4]`. If you'd rather the extra cent go to the first elements by size for refunds (`[-4, -3, -3]`), that's a small change.",
